The communication between back-end developers and front-end developers is often poor, leading to misunderstandings and delays in the development process. This can be especially problematic when it comes to the data that the back-end developer is expected to provide to the front-end developer.

## Solution

To improve communication and reduce misunderstandings, a contract can be created using JSON to describe the information that the back-end developer will make available to the front-end developer. This contract will serve as a clear and concise reference for both teams, ensuring that everyone is on the same page and that the data being provided meets the front-end developer's needs.

